# CSM/CSAL V1 POC manager walkthrough

## What this script is for

Use this while showing these two Databricks notebooks:

1. `CSM CSAL V1 POC V1`
2. `CSM CSAL V1 Ground Truth`

The script follows the actual notebook cells in order. The wording is intentionally conversational, so you can explain the work as a story instead of reading code line by line.

The complete walkthrough takes about 8 to 10 minutes. If the meeting is short, use the one-minute version near the end.

## The story in one line

> We kept production unchanged, separated the booking data by its correct business grain, gave Genie one focused view, and tested it against the same frozen data and independently checked answers.

## Before the meeting

- Open both notebooks before you start.
- Use the saved outputs. There is no need to rerun the whole benchmark during the meeting.
- Keep any customer-level V5 sample values off screen unless your manager specifically asks to see them.
- Keep the final semantic scorecard ready. The final result is `38.9%` for the Wide Baseline and `100%` for the Booking Scope view.
- Do not call the personal schema private. Say it is your personal POC working location.
- Do not say the view was faster. It was slower in this pilot.

