# Opening, about 40 seconds

Say:

> I want to show you a small proof of concept I did for the CSM and CSAL agent.
>
> The question was simple. If Genie gets the full wide Gold table, does it answer booking questions as reliably as when we give it a smaller view designed for one clear business grain?
>
> I did not change production. I read one frozen production snapshot and created all POC objects in my personal Databricks schema. Then I asked both Genie spaces the same questions and checked their answers against independent ground truth.

Then add:

> Also, the problem is not just that the Gold table is wide. Spark can handle many columns. The concern is that allocation, booking outcomes, and commitment values are present at different grains. That can repeat values and give the agent multiple ways to interpret a simple question.

