# Recommendation and closing

Say:

> My recommendation is not to replace the production Gold table and not to migrate everything into a star schema immediately.
>
> I would keep the existing Gold table for current consumers and add small, governed semantic views for Genie one business domain at a time. Each view should have one declared grain, clear column names, and its own verified benchmark before it is connected to an agent.
>
> This V1 proves the Booking Scope view pattern for six booking-focused questions. It does not yet prove MQC, CRM, trends, cross-fact questions, threshold calibration, or executable swap recommendations.

Final line:

> So the simple outcome is that we left production unchanged, tested both designs on the same frozen data, and the focused Booking Scope view improved semantic correctness from 38.9 percent to 100 percent for this limited test, with full repeatability but no latency improvement.

