# One-minute version

> I tested whether Genie performs better on our wide CSM and CSAL Gold structure or on one smaller booking-focused view.
>
> I did not change production. I used a frozen Delta version 38 snapshot with 242,370 rows and built the POC only in my personal schema. I separated allocation, booking outcomes, and commitment values by their correct grains, validated the keys and TEU reconciliations, and created a 29-column Booking Scope view with 238,392 rows.
>
> Then I compared two isolated Genie spaces using the same six questions three times each. The Wide Baseline produced 7 correct runs out of 18, or 38.9 percent. The Booking Scope view produced 18 out of 18, or 100 percent. It was also stable for all six question groups.
>
> The focused view was not faster. Its median latency was 24.3 seconds compared with 18.1 seconds for the wide baseline. So the proven improvement is correctness and consistency, not speed.
>
> My recommendation is to keep production unchanged and add small, tested semantic views gradually, one domain at a time.

